@startuml FRQ-MET-01-attachment
' Priključak na zatečeni okvir, i odnos prema core sučeljima.
' Gledište: integracija. Publika: arhitekt, implementator.
' Prikaz, ne izvor istine (D-13).
title FRQ-MET-01 — Attachment: what is reused, what is deliberately not

skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FEFEFE
  BorderColor #555555
  ArrowColor #555555
}
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
hide empty members

package "existing — untouched" #EEF4FF {
  class Audit <<ILogger, IObserver>> {
    +subscribe_handler(handler)
    +debug() / info() / warning()
  }
  class GenericWorkflow <<IOriginator>> {
    -_connections : ConnectionManager
    -_drivers : DriverManager
    -_processors : ProcessorManager
  }
  class DriverManager <<IObserver>>
  class ConnectionManager <<IObserver>>
  class GenericDriver <<IDriver, IObserver>>
  class GenericProcessor <<IProcessor>>
  class DriverPrometheus
  class DriverGrafana
}

package "new" #F2FBF4 {
  class MetricCollector <<Handler>>
  class MetricReporter
  class PrometheusSink
  class GrafanaSink
}

Audit ..> MetricCollector : subscribe_handler()\n(existing socket)
GenericDriver ..> Audit : Started / Completed | Failed
GenericProcessor ..> Audit : Started / Completed | Failed

GenericWorkflow *-- MetricReporter : owns, closes the run >
DriverManager o-- MetricReporter : optional
ConnectionManager o-- MetricReporter : optional
MetricReporter *-- MetricCollector
MetricReporter o-- PrometheusSink
MetricReporter o-- GrafanaSink
PrometheusSink --> DriverPrometheus : write(job, exposition)
GrafanaSink --> DriverGrafana : write("annotation", ...)

note as N1
  **Reused, because the contract fits**

  · `Audit.subscribe_handler` — the attachment
    point already exists; nothing is added to it.
  · The fan-out shape of `RepositoryWithDriver`
    (strategy + driver, N destinations over one
    subject) — reused as a SHAPE.
  · Transport stays a driver's job: the sink
    formats, the driver ships (FRQ-PRC-15.22).
end note

note as N2
  **Deliberately NOT reused**

  · `IRepository` — its contract is
    `read(identifier) -> ITarget`; a metric is
    not a document and has no identity to read
    back. Naming it a repository would borrow
    the word without the mechanism.
  · `StrategyWrite` — `execute(caller, facade)`
    asserts `ITarget`. Samples are not facades.
  · `IObserver` on the collector — it receives
    log RECORDS, not domain events. `IEvent`
    has no implementation in the tree, so
    typing it that way would be aspiration.
end note

note as N3
  **Distribution boundary (§7.1)**

  Everything left of the sinks imports only
  stdlib + wattleflow, so it stays in the clean
  core. The two sinks name Prometheus and
  Grafana drivers, so they live in
  `wattleflow-processors`, which is already
  outside the zero-trust scope (§7.4).
end note

MetricReporter .. N1
MetricReporter .. N2
PrometheusSink .. N3

@enduml
